Find the area of this trapezium.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(4.5,0)--(3.5,2)--(1,2)--cycle;
\path (2.25,0) node[below] {$11\text{ cm}$};
\path (2.25,2) node[above] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw[->] (0.6,0)--(1.1,0);
\draw[->] (1.3,2)--(1.8,2);
\draw[dashed] (2.5,0)--(2.5,2);
\path (2.5,1) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=2pt] {$4.5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.25,0)--(2.25,0.25)--(2.5,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the area of this trapezium.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,3.5)--(2.625,3.5)--(2.625,1.75)--cycle;
\path (0,1.75) node[left] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (2.625,2.625) node[right,xshift=6mm] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.3125,3.5) node[above] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw[->] (0,2.3)--(0,2.8);
\draw[->] (2.625,2.1)--(2.625,2.6);
\draw (0,3.25)--(0.25,3.25)--(0.25,3.5);
\draw (2.375,3.5)--(2.375,3.25)--(2.625,3.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the area of this trapezium in square metres. The diagram is not to scale.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\begin{scope}[rotate=25]
\draw (0,0)--(4,0)--(3.2,2)--(0.8,2)--cycle;
\path (2,0) node[below right] {$280\text{ cm}$};
\path (2,2) node[above left] {$1.2\text{ m}$};
\draw[->] (0.5,0)--(1,0);
\draw[->] (1.1,2)--(1.6,2);
\draw[dashed] (2.2,0)--(2.2,2);
\path (2.2,1) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=2pt] {$1.8\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.95,0)--(1.95,0.25)--(2.2,0.25);
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
